{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>When you take.</b> In the second year, as it is written in the parashah of Bamidbar, 'in the second year' etc. — 'Take the sum of all the congregation of the children of Israel.' For 'כי תשא' implies the future, while 'ושאו' (and you shall take) implies immediately. And this parashah was stated from the first of Adar, in order to make known the shekels for the terumah of the Tent, to purchase the offerings to sacrifice from the first of Nisan onward, when the Tabernacle was erected. And the language proves it: 'and you shall give for the service of the Tent of Meeting' — from which we learn that the Tent of Meeting was already entirely made. 'And they shall give, each one, the ransom of his soul' — for the needs of the offerings that come for atonement, as Rashi explained. 'And there shall be no plague among them' — when you count them in the second year, because they have already given each one a ransom, the redemption of his soul. For we find in the case of David that there was a plague in Israel when they were counted. And further, as they said: no blessing is found either in a counted thing or in a measured thing — here He promised, 'and there shall be no plague among them,' because the atonement prevents the pestilence. And there are interpreters who say: 'and there shall be no plague among them' — they shall not fall before their enemies. <b>When you count them</b> — when they go out to war."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:14.895729316Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}